nodes.body:
Rebased onto current main and reworked; the description has the updated validation (before/after reproducer on 2×A100, plus the existing shutdown suites).

@njhill this follows the approach you suggested on #34816 ("set the shutdown flag and then kill after some delay"). Could you take a look when you have a moment?
cc @markmc for the drain/abort semantics on parent death (RFC #24885), and @simon-mo since #52299 touches the same run_engine_core region, it applies cleanly on top of this.

Rebased onto the latest main; no conflicts and the patch is unchanged. It composes with #52299, which landed this week: #52299 handles SIGTERM during engine init, and this PR handles the parent dying, including a SIGKILL during init where no SIGTERM ever arrives.

Thanks @vinitrbl for testing `vllm run-batch`! I added it to the description.

@andyxning thanks for picking this up. It's ready for review whenever you have time.

